-- Music area: 45 classic tracker modules from the '90s scene, linked to The Mod Archive
-- (streamed through /dl/ like the Game Pack), plus MUSIC.NFO crediting every artist.
INSERT INTO files (area_id, filename, descr, size, uploader, uploaded_at, status, free, content, ctype) VALUES (5, 'MUSIC.NFO', 'READ ME: the music pack, who made it, how to play it', 3932, 'SysOp', 1792627200000, 'approved', 1, '===============================================================================
       T H E   S E P T I C   T A N K Z   ::   M U S I C   A R E A
        45 tracker modules from the ''90s scene, the stuff we all leeched
===============================================================================

 WHAT ARE THESE FILES?
 ---------------------
 Before MP3s, music on BBSes came as "modules": a tiny song file holding its
 own instrument samples plus the notes to play them, so a 4-minute song fit
 in 100K. You played them back on your Sound Blaster or Gravis Ultrasound.

   .MOD   Amiga ProTracker format, 4 channels (later 6, 8 or more). The
          original. Mostly 1987-1993.
   .S3M   Scream Tracker 3 (Future Crew, 1994). The PC demoscene standard.
   .XM    FastTracker 2 (Triton, 1994). Instruments with envelopes.
   .IT    Impulse Tracker (Jeffrey Lim, 1995). The power user''s choice.

 There''s no MIDI in here on purpose. Almost every .MID file passed around
 on boards back then was somebody''s unlicensed sequence of a pop song.
 Modules were different: original music the scene wrote and spread for free.

 HOW TO PLAY THEM TODAY
 ----------------------
   Windows:  OpenMPT (free, plays and edits everything), or foobar2000 /
             XMPlay.  Mac:  VLC plays all four formats.  Schism Tracker
             (Mac/Win/Linux) and MilkyTracker (Mac/Win, best for MOD/XM)
             let you watch the patterns scroll the way we used to.

 WHO MADE THEM
 -------------
 Every module comes from The Mod Archive (modarchive.org), which has kept
 the scene''s music online since 1996. The board fetches each file from
 there when you download it. All music is the work of its composers,
 credited below. Shared here non-commercially, in the spirit it was
 released. Composers who want a track pulled: leave the SysOp a message.

  Purple Motion (Future Crew) ... Unreal II (Second Reality soundtrack),
                                  Satellite One, Starshine, Aquaphobia,
                                  Astraying Voyages, Sundance, When the
                                  Heavens Fall, Shadowrun, Cool City 1.2
  Skaven (Future Crew) .......... The 2nd Reality, Catch That Goblin!!,
                                  Deep in Her Eyes (Assembly ''94),
                                  Ice Frontier, Realm of Chaos
  Necros ........................ Point of Departure, Ascent of the Cloud
                                  Eagle, Mechanism Eight
  Necros & Purple Motion ........ Click
  Necros & Basehead ............. Search for the Lost Riff
  Captain ....................... Space Debris
  Horace Wimp ................... Hymn to Aurora
  Jogeir Liljedahl .............. Guitar Slinger, Ambrozia
  Jester ........................ Elysium, Stardust Memories
                                  (licensed CC BY-NC-SA)
  Elwood ........................ Dead Lock, Sick on Monday, Into the
                                  Shadow
  Karsten Koch .................. Aryx
  Firefox ....................... Musiklinjen
  Jugi (Complex) ................ Dope (The Party ''95 demo winner)
  Walkman ....................... Klisje paa klisje
  Romeo Knight .................. Cream of the Earth
  Lizardking .................... Age of Legends
  Dr. Awesome ................... 12th Warrior, Andante
  Moby .......................... Elektric Funk
  Andreas Viklund ............... Dreams (licensed CC BY)
  Acumen ........................ One of a Kind (licensed CC BY-NC-ND)
  ArchAngel ..................... Archons of Light
  Jeroen Tel .................... Letting Go
  Nightbeat ..................... Anthem
  Awesome ....................... Aquarium (16 bit)
  Swallow ....................... Butterfly Flew Away
  BeaT .......................... Celestial Fantasia

 Got a module you wrote back then? Upload it. Your own work only.
===============================================================================
', 'text/plain');
